Nethack deities tend to be lazy. Rather than telling the hero to go down 5 
levels and look for the owner of the artifact when you wish for it I think 
they would probably just summon Ashikaga Takauji wielding the Tsurugi of 
Muramasa so you can pick your gift up directly. For prayer gifts this also 
avoids any question of you deciding you aren't interested in the idea of a 
quest for some worthless artifact, you kind of have to pay attention.

As has been suggested before a wish for DSM should come still in use on its 
original owner (which might also be carrying a ?eA). Spellbooks could 
arrive along with a high priest.

So much more fun when you find an altar or a magic lamp on level 1 and have 
to decide whether an early sacrifice or wish is worth the risk...


